From 56941786bf67aa7544e7cb602a034d688a217886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 00:14:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3352/3799] soh: rename func_800E651C -> AudioThread_SetSeqIo

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence GUESS) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: queues an 0xFD command carrying one byte field and the caller's value
Defined in soh/src/code/audio_thread.c.

Tagged [LLM:GUESS] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/audio_thread.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
index 7d72034a1..57e8c477f 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/audio_thread.c
@@ -781,7 +781,8 @@ void AudioThread_ClearChannelIo(void) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32(0xFA000000, 0);
 }
 
-void func_800E651C(u32 arg0, s32 arg1) {
+// LLM generated name (GUESS), was func_800E651C: queues an 0xFD command carrying one byte field and the caller's value
+void AudioThread_SetSeqIo(u32 arg0, s32 arg1) {
     Audio_QueueCmdS32((arg1 & 0xFF) | 0xFD000000, arg0);
 }
 
